 "▼ Dive in: <0>Deterministic?</0>": "",
 "Ordinary software is <0>deterministic</0>: same input, same output, by rules someone wrote. An LLM is <1>probabilistic</1>: it samples from learned patterns.": "",
 "Use each for what it is good at — and often combine them: the LLM decides, ordinary code executes.": "",
 "A database returns exactly what was stored; an LLM generates plausible text and may \"hallucinate\".": "",
 "Search finds existing documents; an LLM composes new text. RAG (Part II) joins the two.": "",
